I left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0`, and the request needs `http-client`, which is outside that grant. It would also send the tick's `reason` text to an external host, and discarding the response doesn't change that. If you want the fetch, the node's authority has to be widened through the graph definition first.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{tick, run-info};

    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(tick: tick) -> run-info;
}
```

